\"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"id\": \"12d2d28fcbab7786\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.333367117307912, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14082905329701723, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7826226, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8757264a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 20034, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 7244, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-05]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Optimize histogram reservoir (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7443)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7443  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-02T13:56:40Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-15T15:00:11Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-15T14:59:34Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_histogram_reservoir` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +173 / -61 across 8 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis improves the concurrent performance of the histogram reservoir's Offer function by 4x (i.e. 75% reduction).\\n\\nAccomplish this by locking each measurement, rather than locking around the entire storage.  Also, defer extracting the trace context from context.Context until collection time. This improves the performance of Offer, which is on the measure hot path.  Exemplars are often overwritten, so deferring the operation until Collect reduces the overall work.\\n\\n```\\n\\n                           │   main.txt   │              hist.txt              │\\n\\n                           │    sec/op    │   sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nFixedSizeReservoirOffer-24    211.4n ± 3%   177.5n ± 3%  -16.04% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nHistogramReservoirOffer-24   200.85n ± 2%   47.41n ± 2%  -76.40% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\ngeomean                       206.1n        91.73n       -55.48%\\n\\n```\\n\\nBenchmarks for Measure:\\n\\n```\\n\\n                                                                                 │  main.txt   │             histres.txt             │\\n\\n                                                                                 │   sec/op    │    sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsEnabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/0-24                 436.7n ± 4%   114.8n ±  5%  -73.72% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsEnabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/10-24                472.2n ± 2%   169.7n ±  8%  -64.08% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 05 pull request optim histogram reservoir open telemetri opentelemetri go 7443 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7443 author dashpol creat 2025 10 02t13 56 40z updat 2025 12 15t15 00 11z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 15t14 59 34z branch optim _ histogram _ reservoir main chang 173 61 across 8 file label mileston v1 400 descript this improv the concurr perform of the histogram reservoir s offer function by 4x i e 75 reduct accomplish this by lock each measur rather than lock around the entir storag also defer extract the trace context from context context until collect time this improv the perform of offer which is on the measur hot path exemplar are often overwritten so defer the oper until collect reduc the overal work main txt hist txt sec op sec op v base fixedsizereservoiroff 24 211 4n 3 177 5n 316 04 p 0 002 n 6 histogramreservoiroff 24 200 85n 247 41n 2 76 40 p 0 002 n 6 geomean 206 1n 91 73n 55 48 benchmark for measur main txt histr txt sec op sec op v base syncmeasur noview exemplarsen int64histogram attribut 0 24 436 7n 4 114 8n 5 73 72 p 0 002 n 6 syncmeasur noview exemplarsen int64histogram attribut 1024 472 2n 2 169 7n 8 64 08 p 0 002 n 6\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8757264a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"id\": \"bcdaee6c0a13a293\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33175234930791203, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1408290532970172, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77724004, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8757264a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 20034, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 7244, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Not sure why coverage is failing\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-12-09T16:57:34Z\\n\\n> Not sure why coverage is failing\\n\\nI think the changes are just exposing an area where we have had coverage overlap. I think this has more to do with how we merge coverage instead of the changes here.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-12-09T17:10:55Z\\n\\nLikely worth looking into using [Go 1.20 coverage directory feature](https://go.dev/doc/go1.20#cover) to replace our current approach.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dashpole** — 2025-12-11T16:49:43Z\\n\\nSeems to have resolved itself.  Now just links are failing (503s from github due to outage).\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-06]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map and atomics for fixed bucket histograms (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7474)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7474  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-08T14:31:21Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-11T16:56:31Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-11T16:56:04Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_syncmap_histogram` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +560 / -201 across 7 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Reviews (31)\\n\\n**MrAlias** — COMMENTED — 2025-10-08T22:17:45Z\\n\\n**dashpole** — COMMENTED — 2025-10-09T12:40:04Z\\n\\n**dashpole** — COMMENTED — 2025-10-09T18:29:01Z\\n\\n**MrAlias** — COMMENTED — 2025-10-10T15:21:23Z\\n\\n**MrAlias** — COMMENTED — 2025-10-10T16:08:31Z\\n\\n**dashpole** — COMMENTED — 2025-10-10T18:14:37Z\\n\\n**dashpole** — COMMENTED — 2025-10-10T18:18:00Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"not sure whi coverag is fail mralia 2025 12 09t16 57 34z not sure whi coverag is fail i think the chang are just expos an area where we have had coverag overlap i think this ha more to do with how we merg coverag instead of the chang here mralia 2025 12 09t17 10 55z like worth look into use go 120 coverag directori featur http go dev doc go1 20 cover to replac our current approach dashpol 2025 12 11t16 49 43z seem to have resolv itself now just link are fail 503s from github due to outag sourc id src pr 06 pull request use sync map and atom for fix bucket histogram open telemetri opentelemetri go 7474 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7474 author dashpol creat 2025 10 08t14 31 21z updat 2025 12 11t16 56 31z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 11t16 56 04z branch optim _ syncmap _ histogram main chang 560 201 across 7 file label mileston v1 400 review 31 mralia comment 2025 10 08t22 17 45z dashpol comment 2025 10 09t12 40 04z dashpol comment 2025 10 09t18 29 01z mralia comment 2025 10 10t15 21 23z mralia comment 2025 10 10t16 08 31z dashpol comment 2025 10 10t18 14 37z dashpol comment 2025 10 10t18 18 00z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"id\": \"b09e2a3b5058dacd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.331505527307912, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1408290532970172, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7764173, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 32141, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 11686, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"My proposal is to not use `span.RecordError` for **terminating errors** per [recording errors on spans semantic conventions](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans).\\n\\nDuring the SIG meeting, it was also noted that `span.RecordError` captures a stack trace. However, since the stack trace reflects where the error was recorded, not where it originated, I don’t find it particularly valuable. Additionally, capturing and emitting a stack trace has a performance cost. In most languages with exception handling (such as Java or .NET), the stack trace is already included in the thrown exception so the cost of capturing the stack trace was already taken and the stack trace is taken in the place where the exception was thrown.\\n\\n> @pellared does that mean span.RecordError should essentially never be called by instrumentation, since panic recovery is already handled by the SDK? Almost makes it seem like we should deprecate RecordError in the API,\\n\\nI believe [`span.RecordError`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/api.md#record-exception) remains valuable, particularly for **non-terminating errors**. A common use case is **retry logic**, where errors occur but don't immediately end the span. This is especially relevant in the context of **custom instrumentation**, where developers have full control and can explicitly record such intermediate errors.\\n\\nWhile instrumentation libraries typically just return errors, they could also benefit from `span.RecordError` if the underlying library provides hooks into retry or failure logic. In such cases, recording retry attempts as span events via `span.RecordError` gives users better visibility into transient issues **without prematurely ending the span**.\\n\\nFor these reasons, I don’t think `span.RecordError` should be deprecated. It might be worth capturing these use cases in the [error recording semantic conventions](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md) (cc @lmolkova).\\n\\nSide note: There is an OTEP https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/pull/4333 that proposes to record exceptions/errors as log records instead of span events.\\n\\n>  and document that End should handle recording exceptions for panics.\\n\\nI think that documenting that `span.End` should handle recording exceptions for panics is a good idea.\\n\\nIn my opinion, this is how we implement [recording an exception](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/exceptions.md#recording-an-exception) in the most possible user-friendly way.\\n\", \"content_